/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:174:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:175:Move magenta particles along corridors formed by parallel colored bars.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:176:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:177:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:178:- bg=7. Particles=6 in col 0. Colored bars on even rows form corridors on odd rows.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:179:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:180:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:181:- Particle goes straight through bg cells.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:182:- When blocked by a colored cell, turns 90° into the perpendicular direction
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:183:  that has a bg cell flanked by same-color bars. Stops at grid edge or full blockage.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:184:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:185:Key insight: Same-color parallel bars define the only valid corridors, so each particle follows a deterministic local trace.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:186:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:187:</reference_puzzle>
