/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:209:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:210:Stamp translated copies of a monochrome template guided by a singleton pixel layout.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:211:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:212:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:213:- bg = background. A large monochrome shape (template, color T).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:214:- Singleton pixels elsewhere: exactly one is color T (layout origin); the rest share color O (overlap color).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:215:- Singletons sit on a uniform-spacing lattice.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:216:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:217:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:218:- Convert each singleton's offset from the origin into coarse lattice units.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:219:- Place a template copy at each offset, scaled by template height/width.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:220:- The origin's copy is painted O instead of T.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:221:- Any pixel covered by two or more copies is also recolored to O.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:222:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:223:Key insight: The single T-colored singleton identifies both the origin position and the "self" copy, which is uniquely recolored.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:224:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:225:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:226:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:227:<reference_puzzle index="13" source="eval" puzzle_id="8698868d" lines="9-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:228:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:229:Match sprites to frames by connected-hole count, then nest each sprite inside its frame.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:230:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:231:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:232:- bg = azure (8). Large hollow squares (frames) arranged in a grid; smaller filled squares (sprites) placed elsewhere.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:233:- Each frame and sprite has a distinct color. Sprites may contain holes (non-sprite-color pixels).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:234:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:235:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:236:- Frames form a regular grid; some may be bg-colored (invisible).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:237:- Count connected hole regions inside each frame's interior and each sprite.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:238:- Pair each frame with the sprite sharing the same hole count.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:239:- Place the matched sprite inside the frame border; recolor sprite holes to the frame's color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:240:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:241:Key insight: The matching key is the number of connected hole components, not hole area or color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:242:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:243:</reference_puzzle>
