/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:263:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:264:Simulate particles along a path with alternating turn direction at collisions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:265:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:266:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:267:- Top-left: 2x2 monochrome blocks define a repeating color cycle (left-to-right).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:268:- Isolated single pixels of a cycle color: start markers adjacent to the path.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:269:- A 2x2 monochrome block of a distinct color: end marker.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:270:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:271:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:272:- Each start marker launches a particle moving straight, painting cycle colors in order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:273:- On hitting a boundary, paint that cell with the end color and turn 90°.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:274:- Turn direction alternates: odd collisions → left (CCW), even → right (CW).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:275:- If the scheduled turn is blocked, the particle stops.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:276:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:277:Key insight: The alternating left/right turn rule is the core mechanism; without it the path would be trivial.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:278:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:279:</reference_puzzle>
