/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:299:<reference_puzzle index="17" source="eval" puzzle_id="4a21e3da" lines="8-20">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:300:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:301:Cut a sprite along border-control rays and slide pieces to grid corners.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:302:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:303:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:304:- bg, fg (main object, ~centered), ctrl (1-2 pixels on grid edges).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:305:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:306:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:307:- Draw rays inward from each ctrl pixel along its row/col, painting only bg cells up to the farthest fg pixel (intermittent).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:308:- Rays partition the grid; fg on the cut line stays in place.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:309:- Cut pieces in regions touching a control edge slide to that corner; others vanish.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:310:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:311:Key insight: Only regions sharing a border edge with a control pixel keep their piece; the ray skips fg cells.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:312:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:313:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:314:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:315:<reference_puzzle index="18" source="eval" puzzle_id="6e453dd6" lines="39-52">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:316:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:317:Slide black shapes rightward to a grey separator, then shoot red rays from enclosed holes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:318:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:319:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:320:- A vertical grey (5) separator column divides the grid into left and right halves.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:321:- Black shapes sit on the left side against a background color (bg).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:322:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:323:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:324:- Translate each black connected component rightward until its right edge is flush with the separator.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:325:- After sliding, find enclosed bg regions (holes) within the black shapes that touch the column just left of the separator.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:326:- For each row spanned by such a hole, emit a red ray across the entire right half of the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:327:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:328:Key insight: Only holes adjacent to the separator trigger rays — the sliding creates enclosures that act as "nozzles" projecting rightward.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:329:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed309175298/1/prompt.md:330:</reference_puzzle>
